    <summary>Copies mail from a Microsoft 365 or personal Outlook account into a PST file on the local disk, keeping folders and attachments, as an Office 365 backup you control.</summary>
    <description>This package installs Email Backup Tool for Microsoft 365 and Outlook, a Windows program for Office 365 backup to a local PST file. It signs in to the mailbox through the Microsoft OAuth 2.0 page with read-only mail access, downloads the selected folders and writes them into an Outlook data file on the PC. No agent, cloud storage or service account is involved, and the sign-in token is never written to disk.

![Email Backup &amp; Migration Tool for Microsoft Office 365 and Outlook screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/m365/m365-v1-main.png)

## How to use Email Backup Tool for Microsoft 365 and Outlook

1. Launch the program and read the start screen, which states what is accessed and that nothing goes to our servers.
2. Press Sign in and approve read access to mail in the Microsoft window.
3. Tick folders in the mailbox tree and check messages in the preview.
4. Limit the copy by dates if needed, pick the destination folder and press Start.

Trial note: before registration each selected folder contributes only its 25 newest emails, and the PST name gets a -trial suffix. A license removes the per-folder cap.

![Email Backup &amp; Migration Tool for Microsoft Office 365 and Outlook screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/m365/m365-v1-filter.png)

## What the Microsoft 365 backup writes

- A Unicode PST with the mailbox folder tree, HTML bodies, sender and recipients, dates, read state and byte-exact attachments.
- Progress that survives a dropped connection. Downloaded items wait in a .download folder beside the PST until it is built.
- A closing summary that counts messages written, skipped, failed or left out by the date filter, so no mail goes missing silently.

Scope: mail only. Gmail, shared mailboxes, contacts, calendar, scheduled runs and a command line are outside this version, so each Office 365 backup is started by hand.

![Email Backup &amp; Migration Tool for Microsoft Office 365 and Outlook screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/m365/m365-v1-run.png)

## Export Office 365 mailbox to PST for data protection

When you export Office 365 mailbox to PST, a deleted folder, a closed account or a long outage no longer means data loss on your side. A complete office 365 backup in a PST lowers that risk. You choose its location, keep it offline to protect it, and recover data later by opening the file in Outlook, with no third-party service provider involved.

## Who needs an Outlook email backup

IT teams who manage an organization's mail and need an outlook email backup for a departing employee, or a retention copy of critical mail before an account is closed. On a work tenant the first sign-in may need admin consent, and the start screen tells the admin what access is requested. Plan on free disk space of roughly one mailbox size.

## Trial and license

This package installs the free trial of a commercial program. Full use needs a license (lifetime, 1-year or business), which removes the 25-message limit per folder. Licensing details sit on the [Office 365 backup software](https://www.softorbits.net/office-365-backup-software/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) page.

## FAQ

### How much does a Microsoft 365 backup cost?

With this tool you pay for one license, lifetime, 1-year or business, and no fee is charged per mailbox. Cloud backup services usually bill for every user instead.

### Which Office 365 backup solution keeps mail on my own PC?

A desktop one such as this program, which backs up the mailbox to a PST file on your disk instead of a vendor's cloud storage. Recovery later means opening that PST in Outlook.

### Where does this tool save an Outlook email backup?

In the destination folder you pick before pressing Start, as a PST file. If that folder syncs to OneDrive, Dropbox or Google Drive, the program warns you first.
